          "task_id": "case-evolve-005",
          "reason": "The prior team has successful historical support and should be preserved, but the failed run exposed a missing implementation role: verification alone produced a broadly passing change while the required behavior remained unaddressed. Adding an implementer strengthens the reusable pattern without removing either established member.",
          "family_description": "A source-based investigation pattern in which one member gathers precise, provenance-backed evidence and another independently cross-checks claims and reconciles discrepancies. It suits tasks requiring answers assembled from multiple external references, with conclusions grounded in traceable evidence and explicit verification; it is less applicable when the work is primarily artifact construction or implementation.",
          "changed_at": "2026-09-04T02:33:12.027923+00:00"
        },
        {
          "version": 2,
          "members": [
            {
              "agent_id": "researcher",
              "role": "evidence_researcher"
            },
            {
              "agent_id": "implementer",
              "role": "implementer"
            },
            {
              "agent_id": "verifier",
              "role": "verifier"
            }
          ],
          "task_id": "case-evolve-006",
          "reason": "The current run demonstrates that implementation and verification alone did not reliably establish the required behavior: the targeted compatibility cases failed, broad regressions appeared, and an unavailable runtime limited validation. The reusable pattern should therefore add a context-analysis role to trace dependency and environment-sensitive behavior before implementation, while retaining the historically supported researcher, implementer, and verifier; there is no evidence that any existing member is persistently mismatched or redundant.",
          "family_description": "A collaborative pattern combining authoritative evidence gathering, direct artifact modification, and independent verification. The members complement one another by separating factual grounding from implementation and from objective checks, with conclusions supported by reproducible evidence, regression coverage, and explicit uncertainty. It applies to compatibility, maintenance, and other change-oriented investigations where a validated artifact is required, but not to purely advisory analysis with no artifact to modify.",
          "changed_at": "2026-09-04T02:41:51.500874+00:00"
        }
      ],
